# Build-time secrets — copy to `.env` for local builds, and set the same
# values in the Netlify dashboard under Site settings → Environment variables.
# These are read by src/lib/portfolio.ts at build time to populate the
# /portfolio pages from the shared Supabase project. If either is missing,
# the build still succeeds and the portfolio falls back to its empty state.
#
# The mail-in request form (src/lib/supabase-public-config.ts) uses the same two
# values and renders them into the page. The ANON key is public by design. The
# build fails if this holds a service-role/secret key. The service-role key is
# never used by this site; don't add it here or to Netlify.

SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxxxxxxxxxxxx.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOi...

# Shipping estimates on /mail-in-repair/start. Server-only: read by the Netlify
# Function at netlify/functions/shipping-estimate.ts, never by the browser.
# Use an EasyPost TEST key (starts with EZTK) until launch. Do NOT prefix it
# with VITE_ — that would bundle it into client code. If it's missing, the
# form still works and shows "roughly" estimates from the zone table.
EASYPOST_KEY=EZTK...
